module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Flatness.Flattening.NilpotentFlatteningDescent
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Flat.FlatteningBridge
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Flat.HenselianFlatteningTheorem

/-!
# The henselization core of Claim 1 of the proof of Stacks 05U9

Claim 1 of the proof of Stacks 05U9 at the index `i = 0` of a generic flatness stratification is
the one index the source's induction does not reach: the stratum `S₀ ∖ S₁` is scheme
theoretically dense, and flatness of `N` over `A` has to be produced outright. The source does
that over the henselization `A^h`, where Stacks 05PG supplies a *smallest* flattening ideal and
the two steps of `Stacks.flat_of_least_flattening_of_flat_away` apply.

This file is that step, assembled from the pieces already in the tree.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ResidueFibre.exists_least_flattening_tensorPrime`: the smallest flattening ideal of
  `N' = B' ⊗_B N` over `A^h`, finitely generated, stated for the ambient `A^h`-module structure
  on `N'`.
* `Stacks.flat_of_flat_away_of_flat_quotient_pow`: **the henselization core.** If the ideal
  generated by a finite family `g` of elements of `A` is proper, `N` is flat on each basic open
  `D(g i)`, `N ⧸ JⁿN` is flat over `A ⧸ Jⁿ` for every `n > 0`, and the union of the `D(g i)` is
  scheme theoretically dense, then `N` is flat over `A`.

## Implementation notes

`Module.FlatAtPointSituation.exists_ideal_flat_quotient_iff_le_of_henselian` states its flatness
clause for the `A`-module structure `Module.FlatAtPointSituation.moduleAM`, which is
`Module.compHom _ (algebraMap S.A S.B)`, whereas every consumer in this chapter works with the
ambient `Module A^h (B' ⊗_B N)`. The two instances are propositionally but not definitionally
equal, so `Stacks.ResidueFibre.exists_least_flattening_tensorPrime` rewrites along
`Module.compHom_algebraMap_eq` once and exports the ambient form.

The henselization is obtained from `IsLocalRing.exists_isHenselization_residueField` inside the
proof: nothing in the statement mentions it, and a caller has no reason to choose one.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05U9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05U9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05PG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05PG)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v w

open IsLocalRing TensorProduct

namespace Stacks.ResidueFibre

section Least

attribute [local instance] Algebra.TensorProduct.rightAlgebra

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
variable {B : Type v} [CommRing B] [IsLocalRing B] [Algebra A B]
  [IsLocalHom (algebraMap A B)] [Algebra.EssFiniteType A B]
variable {N : Type w} [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N] [Module B N] [IsScalarTower A B N]

omit [Module A N] [IsScalarTower A B N] in
/-- **The smallest flattening ideal over the henselization, in the ambient module structure.**
Stacks 05PG applied to `Stacks.ResidueFibre.flatAtPointSituation` gives a finitely generated
ideal `I ⊆ A^h` such that, for an ideal `K ⊆ A^h`, the reduction `N' ⧸ KN'` is flat over
`A^h ⧸ K` exactly when `I ⊆ K`, where `N' = B' ⊗_B N`.

Finite generation needs `A^h → B'` essentially of finite presentation, which
`Stacks.ResidueFibre.essentiallyOfFinitePresentation_algebraMap_localizationTensorPrime`
supplies from the same property of `A → B`. -/
theorem exists_least_flattening_tensorPrime [Module.FinitePresentation B N]
    (Ah : Type u) [CommRing Ah] [IsLocalRing Ah] [Algebra A Ah]
    [IsLocalRing.IsHenselization A (ResidueField A) Ah]
    (hB : (algebraMap A B).EssentiallyOfFinitePresentation) :
    ∃ I : Ideal Ah, I.FG ∧ ∀ K : Ideal Ah,
      Module.Flat (Ah ⧸ K)
          ((Localization.AtPrime (tensorPrime (A := A) (B := B) Ah) ⊗[B] N) ⧸
            (K • (⊤ : Submodule Ah
              (Localization.AtPrime (tensorPrime (A := A) (B := B) Ah) ⊗[B] N)))) ↔ I ≤ K := by
  have : HenselianLocalRing Ah :=
    IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.henselian (R := A) (L := ResidueField A) (Rh := Ah)
  have : Algebra.EssFiniteType Ah
      (Localization.AtPrime (tensorPrime (A := A) (B := B) Ah)) :=
    essFiniteType_localizationTensorPrime Ah
  have : Module.Finite (Localization.AtPrime (tensorPrime (A := A) (B := B) Ah))
      (Localization.AtPrime (tensorPrime (A := A) (B := B) Ah) ⊗[B] N) :=
    finite_tensorPrime_tensorProduct Ah N
  obtain ⟨I, hI, hfg⟩ :=
    Module.FlatAtPointSituation.exists_ideal_flat_quotient_iff_le_of_henselian_of_isScalarTower
      Ah (Localization.AtPrime (tensorPrime (A := A) (B := B) Ah))
      (Localization.AtPrime (tensorPrime (A := A) (B := B) Ah) ⊗[B] N)
  exact ⟨I, hfg (essentiallyOfFinitePresentation_algebraMap_localizationTensorPrime Ah hB)
    (finitePresentation_tensorPrime_tensorProduct Ah N), hI⟩

end Least

end Stacks.ResidueFibre

namespace Stacks

/-- **The henselization core of Claim 1 of the proof of Stacks 05U9.** Let `A → B` be a local
homomorphism of local rings which is essentially of finite presentation, and let `N` be a finitely
presented `B`-module. Let `g` be a finite family of elements of `A` generating a proper ideal
`J`, and suppose

* `N` is flat on each basic open `D(g i)` of `Spec A`;
* `N ⧸ JⁿN` is flat over `A ⧸ Jⁿ` for every `n > 0`; and
* the open `⋃ᵢ D(g i)` is scheme theoretically dense in `Spec A`.

Then `N` is flat over `A`.

This is the index `i = 0` of the source's induction, where the stratum is dense and no shorter
stratification is available. `Stacks.flat_of_least_flattening_of_flat_away` is the ring-theoretic
content, but it consumes a *smallest* flattening ideal, which exists only over a henselian base;
so the whole hypothesis is transported to a henselization `A^h` of `A` — `hU` by
`Stacks.ResidueFibre.forall_flat_away_tensorPrime_of_forall_flat_away`, `hpow` by
`Stacks.ResidueFibre.forall_flat_quotient_pow_tensorPrime_of_forall_flat_quotient_pow` and
`hdense` by `Stacks.eq_zero_of_forall_pow_mul_eq_zero_of_flat` — where
`Stacks.ResidueFibre.exists_least_flattening_tensorPrime` supplies the ideal. The resulting
flatness of `N' = B' ⊗_B N` over `A^h` returns to flatness of `N` over `A` by
`Stacks.ResidueFibre.flat_localization_tensorPrime_iff_flat`, `B → B'` being faithfully flat. -/
theorem flat_of_flat_away_of_flat_quotient_pow {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    {B : Type v} [CommRing B] [IsLocalRing B] [Algebra A B] [IsLocalHom (algebraMap A B)]
    [Algebra.EssFiniteType A B] {N : Type w} [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N] [Module B N]
    [IsScalarTower A B N] [Module.FinitePresentation B N]
    (hB : (algebraMap A B).EssentiallyOfFinitePresentation)
    {ι : Type*} [Finite ι] (g : ι → A) (hJtop : Ideal.span (Set.range g) ≠ ⊤)
    (hU : ∀ i, Module.Flat (Localization.Away (g i)) (Localization.Away (g i) ⊗[A] N))
    (hpow : ∀ n : ℕ, 0 < n → Module.Flat (A ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range g) ^ n)
      (N ⧸ ((Ideal.span (Set.range g) ^ n) • (⊤ : Submodule A N))))
    (hdense : ∀ x : A, (∀ i, ∃ n : ℕ, g i ^ n * x = 0) → x = 0) :
    Module.Flat A N := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨Ah, _, _, _, _⟩ := IsLocalRing.exists_isHenselization_residueField A
  have : IsLocalHom (algebraMap A Ah) :=
    IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.isLocalHom (L := ResidueField A)
  have : Module.Flat A Ah := IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.flat (L := ResidueField A)
  obtain ⟨I, hIfg, hI⟩ :=
    ResidueFibre.exists_least_flattening_tensorPrime (A := A) (B := B) (N := N) Ah hB
  refine (ResidueFibre.flat_localization_tensorPrime_iff_flat (A := A) (B := B) (N := N) Ah).mp
    (flat_of_least_flattening_of_flat_away (fun i ↦ algebraMap A Ah (g i)) ?_ I hIfg hI
      (ResidueFibre.forall_flat_away_tensorPrime_of_forall_flat_away Ah g hU)
      (ResidueFibre.forall_flat_quotient_pow_tensorPrime_of_forall_flat_quotient_pow Ah g hpow)
      (fun y hy ↦ eq_zero_of_forall_pow_mul_eq_zero_of_flat g hdense Ah y hy))
  have hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range fun i ↦ algebraMap A Ah (g i)) =
      (Ideal.span (Set.range g)).map (algebraMap A Ah) := by
    rw [Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
    rfl
  have hle : Ideal.span (Set.range fun i ↦ algebraMap A Ah (g i)) ≤ maximalIdeal Ah := by
    rw [hspan]
    exact (Ideal.map_mono (IsLocalRing.le_maximalIdeal hJtop)).trans
      (Module.FlatAtPointSituation.map_maximalIdeal_le (algebraMap A Ah))
  exact fun htop ↦ (maximalIdeal.isMaximal Ah).ne_top (top_le_iff.mp (htop ▸ hle))

end Stacks

end
